  <$data title=Output text="""<$notebook-kit>
<$list filter="[range[5]]">
{{!!type}} <$codeblock code={{!!text}} language={{!!type}} /> <div class="tc-notebook-output" data-tiddler-title=<<currentTiddler>>/>
</$list>
</$notebook-kit>"""/>
  <$data title="1" type="text/x-markdown" text="""# Cell types

The notebook-kit library supports many cell types. The tiddller `type` field is used to determine the type.

- text/x-markdown - markdown
- text/x-typescript - typescript
- application/javascript - javascript
- text/html - html
- text/vnd.graphviz - graphviz dot
- text/x-tex - latex math markup

Javascript string interpolation is performed on all such cells. ${"`${greet}`"} = **${greet}**"""/>
  <$data title="2" type="text/x-typescript" text="""let greet: string = "world";
display(greet)"""/>
  <$data title="3" type="text/html" text="Hello, <b>${greet}</b>"/>
  <$data title="4" type="text/vnd.graphviz" text="digraph { greet -> ${greet} }"/>
  <$data title="5" type="text/x-tex" text="\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-x^2} dx = \sqrt{\pi}"/>
</$testcase>

